Files:
 src/qkz80.cc
 src/qkz80_reg_set.cc
 docs/archive/TNYLPO_ANALYSIS.md
 docs/archive/FLAG_DEBUG_PROGRESS.md
 docs/archive/FLAG_DEBUG_STATUS.md
Copyright:
 2025-2026 Aaron Wohl
 2019 Georg Brein
License: GPL-3+ and BSD-3-clause
Comment:
 The DAA instruction in src/qkz80.cc, and add8_bitwise, sub8_bitwise,
 add16_bitwise and sub16_bitwise in src/qkz80_reg_set.cc, are adapted from
 src/cpu.c of tnylpo by Georg Brein (https://gitlab.com/gbrein/tnylpo),
 under the BSD 3-Clause license.  The rest of each source file is GPL-3+.
 The three notes in docs/archive quote parts of that code.  NOTICE in the
 upstream tree lists the same files.

Files: tests/8080/*
Copyright:
 1994 Frank D. Cringle
 2009 Ian Bartholomew
License: GPL-2+
Comment:
 Frank D. Cringle's Z80 instruction exerciser and preliminary tests, changed
 to exercise an 8080 by Ian Bartholomew in February 2009, as copied from
 https://github.com/superzazu/8080 (cpu_tests).  The headers of the .mac files
 carry Cringle's copyright notice and name Bartholomew as the author of the
 changes; Bartholomew's changes carry no separate notice.  These are test
 programs that run under the emulator.  The .com files are copied, not built
 here; the .prn files are their Microsoft MACRO-80 3.44 listings.

Files:
 tests/zexdoc.com
 tests/zexdoc.mac
 tests/zexall.com
 tests/zexall.mac
Copyright: 1994 Frank D. Cringle
License: GPL-2+
Comment:
 Frank D. Cringle's Z80 instruction set exerciser, from YAZE-AG 2.51.3, as
 published at https://github.com/agn453/ZEXALL.  The .com files are copied
 byte-identical from that repository; the .mac files say to assemble them with
 Hector Peraza's ZSM4.  No other copyright notice is in the files.

